{"id":"debir","name":"Debir","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:debir"],"groups":["2. A town in the mountains of Judah"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Debir","text":"Oracle town; sanctuary. (1.) One of the eleven cities to the west of Hebron, in the highlands of Judah (Josh. 15:49; Judg. 1:11-15). It was originally one of the towns of the Anakim (Josh. 15:15), and was also called Kirjath-sepher (q.v.) and Kirjath-sannah (49). Caleb, who had conquered and taken possession of the town and district of Hebron (Josh. 14:6-15), offered the hand of his daughter to any one who would successfully lead a party against Debir. Othniel, his younger brother (Judg. 1:13; 3:9), achieved the conquest, and gained Achsah as his wife. She was not satisfied with the portion her father gave her, and as she was proceeding toward her new home, she “lighted from off her ass” and said to him, “Give me a blessing [i.e., a dowry]: for thou hast given me a south land” (Josh. 15:19, A.V.); or, as in the Revised Version, “Thou hast set me in the land of the south”, i.e., in the …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","xlit":"Yᵉhôwshûwaʻ","gloss":"Jehoshua , the Jewish leader","kjv":"Jehoshua, Jehoshuah, Joshua","count":17,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H1688","lemma":"דְּבִיר","xlit":"Dᵉbîyr","gloss":"Debir, the name of an Amoritish king and of two places i","kjv":"Debir","count":6,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H4631","lemma":"מְעָרָה","xlit":"mᵉʻârâh","gloss":"a cavern","kjv":"cave, den, hole","count":6,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H7158","lemma":"קִרְיַת סַנָּה","xlit":"Qiryath Çannâh","gloss":"Kirjath-Sannah or Kirjath-Sepher, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Kirjath-sannah, Kirjath-sepher","count":4,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H5915","lemma":"עַכְסָה","xlit":"ʻAkçâh","gloss":"Aksah, an Israelitess","kjv":"Achsah","count":4,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H1391","lemma":"גִּבְעוֹן","xlit":"Gibʻôwn","gloss":"Gibon, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Gibeon","count":5,"share":0.15}],"v